{t: Pecan Pie}
{st: Jeff Tweedy}
{key: G}
{tempo: 128}

{sot: Verse}
| G           | C           | G           | C           |
| G           | C           | G           | C           |
{eot}

{sot: Chorus}
| C     C/F#  | G     D     | C     C/F#  | G     D     |
| C     C/F#  | G     D     | C     C/F#  | G     D     |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Golden Smog Side Project: Written and performed by Jeff Tweedy on the 1995
Golden Smog record "Down by the Old Mainstream."

Verse Bass Run: The movement between G and C typically uses an G to A to B
single-note walk-up on the low E and A strings leading directly into the C
open chord.

Chorus Voicing: The C/F# voicing (200010 or 2x2010) adds the signature alt-
country chromatic bass shift as the progression moves toward the G to D
resolution.

Acoustic Strumming: Keep the strumming loose and driving with an upbeat,
folky country-rock feel throughout.
{eov}